m. Contributes to the nuclear and mitochondrial de novo thymidylate biosynthesis pathway (PubMed:21876188, PubMed:22235121). Catalyzes an essential reaction for de novo glycine and purine synthesis, and for DNA precursor synthesis. Binds its own mRNA and that of DHFR2."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"P00374","pdb_id":"1kms","het_id":"NDP","resolution":1.09,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"NADPH","ligand_class":"cofactor or substrate","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"HUMAN DIHYDROFOLATE REDUCTASE COMPLEXED WITH NADPH AND 6-([5-QUINOLYLAMINO]METHYL)-2,4-DIAMINO-5-METHYLPYRIDO[2,3-D]PYRIMIDINE (SRI-9439), A LIPOPHILIC ANTIFOLATE","first_author":"Klon, A.E.","n_authors":7,"journal":"J.Mol.Biol.","year":2002,"doi":"10.1016/S0022-2836(02)00469-2","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-2836(02)00469-2"},{"accession":"P00374","pdb_id":"1kmv","het_id":"NDP","resolution":1.05,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"NADPH","ligand_class":"cofactor or substrate","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"HUMAN DIHYDROFOLATE REDUCTASE COMPLEXED WITH NADPH AND (Z)-6-(2-[2,5-DIMETHOXYPHENYL]ETHEN-1-YL)-2,4-DIAMINO-5-METHYLPYRIDO[2,3-D]PYRIMIDINE (SRI-9662), A LIPOPHILIC ANTIFOLATE","first_author":"Klon, A.E.","n_authors":7,"journal":"J.Mol.Biol.","year":2002,"doi":"10.1016/S0022-2836(02)00469-2","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-2836(02)00469-2"},{"accession":"P00374","pdb_id":"4m6j","het_id":"NDP","resolution":1.201,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"NADPH","ligand_class":"cofactor or substrate","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Crystal structure of human dihydrofolate reductase (DHFR) bound to NADPH","first_au